"**【recipe-service-v2 Affected API Endpoints】**

All affected APIs are defined in the recipe-service-v2-interface module. The change moves the JSON field `is_ik_eligible_selected` from the sub-step (ProcedureStep) level to the step (Procedure) level in every line-build-related response. Request payloads and endpoint paths are unchanged; this is a response-shape (clean cutover) change only.

Affected endpoints (all in ItemWebService):

1. `PUT /item/structure/bulk-get` — bulkGetStructure → BulkGetItemStructureResponse (Stakeholders: WHISK; @Deprecated since 2024 Sprint 26)
1. `PUT /v2/item/line-build/structure/bulk-get` — bulkGetLineBuildStructureV2 → BulkGetItemLineBuildStructureResponseV2 (Stakeholders: KCS)
1. `PUT /item/all-line-build/base-structure/bulk-get` — bulkGetAllLineBuildBaseStructure → BulkGetALLItemLineBuildBaseStructureResponse (Stakeholders: KCS)
1. `BulkGetItemLineBuildStructureResponse (v1)` — DTO class only; not directly returned by any current endpoint, but its inner types are reused by InventoryItemWebService responses (BulkGetInventoryConsumableItemsItemLineBuildView). Still updated for consistency.

JSON Response Shape Change (applies to all 3 endpoints above):

```json
// BEFORE — field on each ProcedureStep (sub-step)
{
  "procedures": [{
    "steps": [{
      "is_ik_eligible_selected": true,
      "is_hot_hold_eligible_selected": false,
      ...
    }]
  }]
}

// AFTER — field moved up to Procedure (step) level
{
  "procedures": [{
    "is_ik_eligible_selected": true,
    "steps": [{
      "is_hot_hold_eligible_selected": false,
      ...
    }]
  }]
}
```

**Test Suggestions for Downstream Stakeholders (WHISK / KCS / Pantry)**

1. Call PUT /v2/item/line-build/structure/bulk-get for a 41* item that has at least one garnish step with IK Eligible = true; verify is*ik*eligible_selected appears under each procedure (not under steps) and value matches what was set on the BO line build edit page.
1. Call PUT /item/all-line-build/base-structure/bulk-get for items with multiple tasks/procedures; verify the field appears once per procedure and is null/absent for non-garnish activities.
1. Call PUT /item/structure/bulk-get (deprecated) and confirm the deprecated response also follows the new field location — to ensure WHISK still consuming the legacy endpoint is not broken.
1. Verify that the steps array inside each procedure no longer contains is*ik*eligible_selected (clean cutover, no dual-shape).
1. Bulk-fetch items that include line*build*snapshots (item*version*snapshots) — note: snapshots are intentionally NOT migrated, so historical snapshot responses may still expose null at procedure level; verify no NPE on serialization.
1. Regression: call PUT /inventory/consumable-items/bulk-get and PUT /v2/inventory/consumable-items/bulk-get (InventoryItemWebService) — these reuse line-build inner DTOs; confirm response still parses and unrelated fields (hotHolds, relatedItems, customizationOption) are unchanged.

(From commits on branch MD-17820: 72acb81b101, 563a02f7a5c, e037cea7b43, d1810007c5c)"

