      "id": "770739",
      "body": "**【What Changed】**\n\nExtended the IK Eligible validation on the line build step level to support COOK activity in addition to GARNISH. Previously, only GARNISH steps could be flagged as IK eligible; cooked components (e.g. steak) can now also be marked, so a step is validated against machine-eligible items when its activity is COOK or GARNISH.\n\nMain changes:\n\n1. Backend save-time validation now treats both COOK and GARNISH procedures as IK-eligible candidates; other activities (COMPLETE, VEND) are skipped.\n1. All existing cook step configurations (appliance, cooking time, etc.) are preserved when the IK Eligible flag is checked, so the a la minute instruction still works when the IK slot is not filled at HDR.\n1. Existing rule unchanged: a step can be checked as IK eligible only when at least one of its sub-step items is machine eligible; otherwise the save is blocked with an error message.\n\n**Technical Details**\n\n  - **Validator:* `IkEligibleMachineEligibleChecker` — activity guard changed from `activity != GARNISH` to `activity != GARNISH && activity != COOK`.\n  - **Flag location:* `is_ik_eligible_selected` lives on the procedure (step) level (per MD-17820), not on sub-steps.\n  - **Trigger path:* called from `ItemLineBuildErrorChecker` during line-build save/validate; uses the MACHINE_ELIGIBLE tag id to identify eligible items in the sub-step.\n  - **Unit test updated:* the negative case in `IkEligibleMachineEligibleCheckerTest` now uses VEND (still ineligible) instead of COOK to verify the skip branch.\n  - **Related frontend:* tracked separately under MD-17982 (UI to show the checkbox on cook steps).\n\n**【Affected Functions】**\n\n1. Menu item line build editing (cook step IK Eligible checkbox)\n1. Line build save / validate flow (backend error checker)\n1. Cook step configurations (appliance, cooking time, a la minute instruction)\n\n**【Test Suggestions】**\n\n1. Edit a menu item line build, set a procedure activity to COOK with at least one machine-eligible sub-step item, check IK Eligible, then save\n1. Edit a COOK step that has NO machine-eligible item in its sub-steps, check IK Eligible, then save\n1. Re-test the existing GARNISH IK eligible flow (with and without machine-eligible sub-step item) to confirm no regression\n1. Edit a COMPLETE / VEND step, attempt to mark IK Eligible (checkbox should not be available; if set via legacy data, validator should skip it)\n1. Mark a COOK step as IK eligible, save, then reopen the line build to confirm the appliance, cooking time and other cook step fields are still present (a la minute path preserved)\n1. Toggle a procedure activity between COOK and GARNISH and confirm the IK Eligible value is preserved across the switch; toggle to a non-eligible activity (e.g. VEND) and confirm IK Eligible is cleared\n1. Use a steak-style menu item: configure IK Eligible on a cook step, save and verify the line build does not add extra pre-cook guidance steps for the CE\n1. Open the line build change history / snapshot of an item that has COOK + IK Eligible and confirm the flag is displayed correctly\n\n(From commits: 597bacf53e2)",
