      "items": [
        {
          "field": "description",
          "fieldtype": "jira",
          "from_string": "h2. Requirement\n\nCurrently, only GARNISH steps can be checked as IK eligible. We need to extend this to Cook activity type.\n\nh3. Core Behavior\n\n# *Enable IK eligible for all activity types*: Allow users to check \"IK eligible\" on any step of cook/garnish activity type.\n# *Trigger*: A step becomes eligible for the IK eligible flag when it has any machine eligible item in its sub-step\n# *Preserve existing configurations*: When a step is marked IK eligible, keep all existing activity step configurations:\n#* For cook steps: retain appliance, cooking time, and other cooking-specific fields\n#* This ensures that if the item is NOT filled in the IK slot at the HDR, the CE can still cook it via a la minute instruction using the existing step configuration\n\nh3. Workflow Example: Steak\n\n* If a steak menu item is configured with IK eligible on a cook step:\n** *IK slot filled at HDR*: The steak is pre-cooked and filled into the IK slot. SOP/off-line training guides CE on how to pre-cook the steak and fill it into the IK slot.\n** *IK slot NOT filled at HDR*: The CE cooks the steak via the existing a la minute instruction using the cook step's appliance and cooking time configuration.\n* The menu item line build will NOT have additional steps to guide the user on how to pre-cook the steak (this is handled by SOP/off-line training)\n\nh2. Acceptance Criteria\n\n# IK eligible checkbox is available and functional for all activity types of steps (cook, vendor, etc.), not just GARNISH\n# A step can be marked IK eligible when it contains at least one machine eligible item in its sub-step\n# Existing activity step configurations (appliance, cooking time, etc.) are preserved when a step is marked IK eligible\n# No additional steps are auto-generated in the line build for IK pre-cooking instructions (handled by SOP/off-line training)",
          "to_string": "h2. Background\n\nCurrently, only GARNISH steps can be checked as IK eligible. However, there are cooked components apply to IK machine. We need to extend this to Cook activity type.\n\nh2. Requirement\n\n# Show \"IK eligible\" checkbox, if the activity type=cook/garnish.\n# A step becomes eligible for the IK eligible flag when it has any machine eligible item in its sub-step. Else, don’t allow user to check the  IK eligible flag, show error message. (existing validation)\n# *Preserve existing configurations*: When a step is marked IK eligible, keep all existing activity step configurations:\n#* Like, cook steps: retain appliance, cooking time, and other cooking-specific fields\n#* This ensures that if the item is NOT filled in the IK slot at the HDR, the CE can still cook it via a la minute instruction using the existing step configuration\n\nh3. Workflow Example: Steak\n\n* If a steak menu item is configured with IK eligible on a cook step:\n** *IK slot filled at HDR*: The steak is pre-cooked and filled into the IK slot. SOP/off-line training guides CE on how to pre-cook the steak and fill it into the IK slot.\n** *IK slot NOT filled at HDR*: The CE cooks the steak via the existing a la minute instruction using the cook step's appliance and cooking time configuration.\n* The menu item line build will NOT have additional steps to guide the user on how to pre-cook the steak (this is handled by SOP/off-line training)"
        }
      ],
